              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Query Reports Utilities Help Log Out\n\nPROTO\n\nU.S. District Court\nDistrict of Hawaii (Hawaii)\nCRIMINAL DOCKET FOR CASE #: 1:23-cr-00071-JMS All Defendants\n\nCase title: USA v. Riley Date Filed: 08/24/2023\n\nAssigned to: JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT\n\nDefendant (1)\nDarren Patrick Riley represented by Andrew M. Kennedy\nSchlueter, Kwiat & Kennedy LLLP\n75-167 Kalani Street Suite 201\nKailua-Kona, HI 96740\n(808) 987-7275\nFax: (808) 443-0339\nEmail: Andrew@kona-lawyer.com\nTERMINATED: 04/10/2026\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nBenjamin E. Lowenthal\nThe Law Office of Benjamin E. Lowenthal\n1001 Bishop Street, Ste 2210\nHonolulu, HI 96813\n808-766-8247\nEmail: benjamin@bellawyer.com\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nGary Gurmail Singh\nTopa Financial Center\nBishop Street Tower\n700 Bishop Street, Ste 2000\nHonolulu, HI 96813\n808-529-0626\nFax: 808-529-0627\nEmail: gary@garysinghlaw.com\nTERMINATED: 08/11/2025\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nHarlan Y. Kimura\nCentral Pacific Plaza\n220 S King St Ste 1660\nHonolulu, HI 96813\n521-4134\nFax: 521-0361\nEmail: hyk@harlankimuralaw.com\nTERMINATED: 01/14/2025\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: CJA Appointment\n\nMelinda K. Yamaga\nOffice of the Federal Public Defender\nPJKK Federal Building\n300 Ala Moana Blvd Rm 7-104\nHonolulu, HI 96850\n808 541-2521\nEmail: Melinda_Yamaga@fd.org\nTERMINATED: 09/09/2024\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender Appointment\n\nCraig W. Jerome\nOffice of the Federal Public Defender\nPJKK Federal Building\n300 Ala Moana Blvd Rm 7-104\nHonolulu, HI 96850\n808 541-2521\nEmail: Craig_Jerome@fd.org\nTERMINATED: 08/30/2023\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Public Defender or Community Defender Appointment\n\nPending Counts Disposition\n18:2251A.F SELLING OR BUYING OF CHILDREN, Production of Child Pornography, 18\nU.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a)\n(1)\n18:2251.F SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN, Production of Child Pornography, 18\nU.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2251(a) and 2251(e)\n(1s)\n18:2252A.F ACTIVITIES RE MATERIAL CONSTITUTING/CONTAINING CHILD\nPORNOGRAPHY, Possession of Child Pornography, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2252(a)(4)(B) and 2252(b)(2)\n(2)\n18:2251.F SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN, Production of Child Pornography, 18\nU.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 225l{a) and 225l(e)\n(2s)\n18:2251.F SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF CHILDREN, Production of Child Pornography, 18\nU.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2251(a) and 2251(e)\n(3s)\n18:1591.F SEX TRAFFICKING OF CHILDREN OR BY FORCE, FRAUD OR COERCION,\nSex Trafficking a Minor, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 1591(a)(l) and 1591(b)(2)\n(4s)\n18:2252.F SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF MINORS, Distribution of Child Pornography, 18\nU.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2252(a)(2) and 2252(b)(l)\n(5s)\n18:1591.F SEX TRAFFICKING OF CHILDREN OR BY FORCE, FRAUD OR COERCION,\nSex Trafficking a Minor, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 159l(a)(l) and 1591(b)(2)\n(6s)\n18:2422.F COERCION OR ENTICEMENT OF FEMALE, Coercion and Enticement of a Minor,\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2422(b)\n(7s)\n18:2252.F SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF MINORS, Receipt of Child Pornography, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\n2252(a)(2)\n(8s)\n18:1591.F SEX TRAFFICKING OF CHILDREN OR BY FORCE, FRAUD OR COERCION,\nSex Trafficking a Minor, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 1591(a)(l) and 1591(b)(2)\n(9s)\n18:2422.F COERCION OR ENTICEMENT OF FEMALE, Coercion and Enticement of a Minor,\n18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2422(b)\n(10s)\n18:1591.F SEX TRAFFICKING OF CHILDREN OR BY FORCE, FRAUD OR COERCION,\nSex Trafficking a Minor, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 1591(a)(l) and 1591(b)(2)\n(11s)\n18:2252.F SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF MINORS, Possession of Child Pornography, 18\nU.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2252(a)(4)(B) and 2252(b)(2)\n(12s)\n\nHighest Offense Level (Opening)\nFelony\n\nTerminated Counts Disposition\nNone\n\nHighest Offense Level (Terminated)\nNone\n\nComplaints Disposition\nNone\n\nPlaintiff\nUSA represented by Rebecca Ann Perlmutter\nOffice of the U.S. Attorney\nPJKK Federal Building, Room 6-100\n300 Ala Moana Boulevard\nHonolulu, HI 96850\n(808) 541-2850\nFax: (808) 541-2958\nEmail: rebecca.perlmutter@usdoj.gov\nLEAD ATTORNEY\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Government\n\nGwendelynn Bills\nU.S. Department of Justice\n1301 New York Avenue N.W.\nWashington, DC 20005\n202-616-2572\nEmail: Gwendelynn.E.Bills@usdoj.gov\nATTORNEY TO BE NOTICED\nDesignation: Government\n\nDate Filed # Docket Text\n08/24/2023 1 INDICTMENT as to Darren Patrick Riley (1) count(s) 1, 2. (eta) (Entered: 08/24/2023)\n08/24/2023 4 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley - An Initial Appearance; Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment is set for 8/28/2023 at 10:30 AM in Courtroom 7 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER. (Attorney Craig\nW. Jerome and the Office of the Federal Public Defender are provisionally appointed as counsel pending submission of defendant's financial affidavit.)\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo)\nModified on 8/28/2023 (jo)\n(Entered: 08/24/2023)\n08/25/2023 5 MOTION to Detain /Certificate of Service by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 08/25/2023)\n08/28/2023 6 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley - Due to Defendant's refusal to be transported to Court today, the Initial Appearance; Arraignment and Plea set for 8/28/2023 is CONTINUED to 8/29/2023 at 10:30 AM in Courtroom 7\nbefore MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 08/28/2023)\n08/29/2023 8 EP: INITIAL APPEARANCE; ARRAIGNMENT AND PLEA to the Indictment as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley not held.\n\nAUSA Rebecca Perlmutter appeared on behalf of the United States.\n\nMr. Craig Jerome appeared on behalf of Defendant.\n\nDefendant not present, as he refused to be transported to court today.\n\nBy agreement of the parties, the Initial Appearance; Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment is continued to September 1, 2023 at 10:30 am in Courtroom 7 with Magistrate Judge Wes Reber Porter.\n\n(FTR-CT 7 / 10:53 am - 10:59 am)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 08/29/2023)\n08/30/2023 10 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE: appearing for Darren Patrick Riley Notice of Change of Counsel (Yamaga, Melinda) (Entered: 08/30/2023)\n09/01/2023 11 EP: INITIAL APPEARANCE; ARRAIGNMENT AND PLEA to the Indictment as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley not held.\n\nAUSA Rebecca Perlmutter appeared on behalf of the United States.\n\nMs. Melinda Yamaga appeared on behalf of Defendant.\n\nDefendant not present, as he refused to be transported to court today.\n\nThe Court FINDS that beginning on August 28, 2023, Defendant has repeatedly denied transportation to attend his Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment. Accordingly, the Court FINDS that the\ntime from August 28, 2023 to September 6, 2023 is excluded from the requirements of Rule 5 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure.\n\nBy agreement of the parties, the Initial Appearance; Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment is continued to September 6, 2023 at 10:30 am in Courtroom 7 with Magistrate Judge Wes Reber Porter.\n\n(FTR-CT 7 / 10:42 am - 10:47 am)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 09/01/2023)\n09/06/2023 13 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley Because Defendant Darren Patrick Riley has refused, for the fourth time, to be transported to Court today, the Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment is VACATED\nand will be reset as appropriate.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 09/06/2023)\n09/28/2023 15 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley - An Initial Appearance; Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment is set for 9/29/2023 at 10:30 AM in Courtroom 7 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 09/28/2023)\n09/28/2023 16 ORDER TO PRODUCE as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER on 9/28/2023.\n\nThe U.S. Marshals Service is ORDERED to bring Defendant to Court, even if the use of reasonable force is necessary.\n\nIT IS FURTHER ORDERED that this Order shall remain in effect for the duration of the pretrial proceedings in this matter.\n\nIT IS FURTHER ORDERED that the Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment is September 29, 2023, at 10:30 a.m. before Magistrate Judge Wes Reber Porter in Courtroom 7 of the United States Courthouse, 300 Ala Moana Blvd.,\nHonolulu, Hawaii.\n\nIT IS FURTHER ORDERED that the United States Attorney's Office shall serve a copy of this Order on (1) the Federal Detention Center, Honolulu and (2) the U.S. Marshals Service no later than 12:00 p.m. noon on Thursday, September 28, 2023.\n\n(eta) (Entered: 09/28/2023)\n09/29/2023 17 EP: INITIAL APPEARANCE; ARRAIGNMENT AND PLEA to the Indictment as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley not held.\n\nAUSA Rebecca Perlmutter appeared on behalf of the United States.\n\nMs. Melinda Yamaga appeared on behalf of Defendant.\n\nDefendant present and in custody.\n\nDiscussion held.\n\n10:47 - 10:55 - Brief recess to allow Counsel to confer with Defendant.\n\nThe Court finds that due to Defendant's demeanor and behavior today, the Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment cannot proceed.\n\nFor the record, the Court further FINDS that beginning on August 28, 2023, Defendant had repeatedly denied transportation to attend his Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment. Accordingly, the\ntime from August 28, 2023 to September 29, 2023 is excluded from the requirements of Rule 5 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure. Furthermore, the Court FINDS the continuous delay shall not be excluded under\nthe Speedy Trial Act.\n\nNo later than October 6, 2023, Ms. Yamaga shall submit a letter to the Court, via email to porter_orders@hid.uscourts.gov and copied to the Government, with a status on her efforts to communicate with the Defendant.\nBased upon the letter, the Court will determine how best to proceed with regard to an Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshal Service.\n\n(FTR-CT 7 / 10:37 am - 10:47 am / 10:56 am - 11:06 am)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 09/29/2023)\n09/29/2023 18 AMENDED EP re: 17 : INITIAL APPEARANCE; ARRAIGNMENT AND PLEA to the Indictment as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley not held.\n\nAUSA Rebecca Perlmutter appeared on behalf of the United States.\n\nMs. Melinda Yamaga appeared on behalf of Defendant.\n\nDefendant present and in custody.\n\nDiscussion held.\n\n10:47 - 10:55 - Brief recess to allow Counsel to confer with Defendant.\n\nThe Court finds that due to Defendant's demeanor and behavior today, the Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment cannot proceed.\n\nFor the record, the Court further FINDS that beginning on August 28, 2023, Defendant had repeatedly denied transportation to attend his Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment. Accordingly, the\ntime from August 28, 2023 to September 29, 2023 is excluded from the requirements of Rule 5 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure. Furthermore, the Court FINDS the continuous delay shall be excluded\nunder the Speedy Trial Act.\n\nNo later than October 6, 2023, Ms. Yamaga shall submit a letter to the Court, via email to porter_orders@hid.uscourts.gov and copied to the Government, with a status on her efforts to communicate with the Defendant.\nBased upon the letter, the Court will determine how best to proceed with regard to an Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshal Service.\n\n(FTR-CT 7 / 10:37 am - 10:47 am / 10:56 am - 11:06 am)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 09/29/2023)\n10/10/2023 19 18 STATUS LETTER from Melinda K. Yamaga dated October 6, 2023. (bbb) (Entered: 10/10/2023)\n10/10/2023 20 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley - Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment is set for 10/11/2023 at 9:30 a.m. in Courtroom 6 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD.\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD)(bbb) (Entered: 10/10/2023)\n10/11/2023 21 EP : Initial Appearance and Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment as to Darren Patrick Riley not held on 10/11/2023. Defendant is not present.\n\nMs. Perlmutter states on the record the incident that occurred at FDC when officers attempted to take Defendant out of his cell to be transported to Court for this court proceedings.\n\nCourt proposes options to move case forward given the Defendant's ongoing refusal to participate in Court proceedings: (1) Defendant may file a signed Waiver of Appearance and Entry of Not Guilty Plea for the Court's\nconsideration; or (2) the Court may hold a Competency Hearing pursuant to 18 U.S.C. section 4241(a). Discussion held. Counsel raised the additional possibility of a (3) Initial Appearance and Arraignment by video\nconference, if FDC is willing to accommodate and the Defendant will participate in that manner.\n\nIf the Defendant agrees, Ms. Yamaga may file a signed Waiver of Appearance and Entry of Not Guilty Plea no later than Tuesday, October 17, 2023. Parties are to file their position on competency no later than close of\nbusiness on Tuesday, October 17, 2023.\n\nInitial Appearance and Arraignment & Plea to Indictment or for Competency Hearing is 10/19/2023 @ 10:30 a.m. before Magistrate Judge Kenneth J. Mansfield in Courtroom 6.\n\nEO: The Court finds that, due to Defendant's ongoing refusal to appear for and participate in his Initial Appearance and Arraignment & Plea to Indictment, the time from September 29, 2023 to October 19, 2023 is\nexcluded from the requirements of Rule 5 of the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure. Furthermore, the Court FINDS the continuous delay shall be excluded under the Speedy Trial Act.\nStatus Conference - MJ as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 10/11/2023.\nArraignment is set for 10/19/2023 10:30 AM in Courtroom 6 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD.\nInitial Appearance is set for 10/19/2023 10:30 AM in Courtroom 6 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD.\nCompetency Hearing is set for 10/19/2023 10:30 AM in Courtroom 6 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD.\n***Excludable started/stopped as to Darren Patrick Riley: 9/29/2023-10/19/2023\n\n(FTR-CT 6 / 9:52-10:05 AM) (MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD)\n(eta) (Entered: 10/12/2023)\n10/17/2023 22 RESPONSE GOVERNMENT'S BRIEF REGARDING POSITION ON COMPETENCY AND DEFENDANT'S STATUS; EXHIBITS A & B; CERTIFICATE OF SERVICE by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley re 21 Status\nConference,,,,,,,,,, Set/Reset Hearings,,,,,,,,,, Speedy Trial - Excludable Start,,,,,,,,,, Speedy Trial - Excludable Stop,,,,,,,,, / Certificate of Service (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit A, # 2 Exhibit B)(Perlmutter, Rebecca) Modified on\n10/19/2023 (jni) (Entered: 10/17/2023)\n\n10/17/2023 23 MOTION to Seal EXHIBIT A AND EXHIBIT B TO GOVERNMENT'S BRIEF REGARDING POSITION ON COMPETENCY AND DEFENDANT'S STATUS / Certificate of Service by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley.\n(Perlmutter, Rebecca) Modified on 10/19/2023 (jni) (Entered: 10/17/2023)\n10/17/2023 24 ORDER re 23 - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD on 10/17/2023.\n\nIT IS HEREBY ORDERED that Exhibit A and Exhibit B to the Government's Brief Regarding Position on Competency and Defendant's Status, which consist entirely of Defendant's medical records, be sealed.\n\n(jni) (Entered: 10/17/2023)\n10/17/2023 25 SEALED EXHIBITS\nEXHIBITS A, B to ECF 22 GOVERNMENT'S BRIEF REGARDING POSITION ON COMPETENCY AND DEFENDANT'S STATUS - by USA.\n(Attachments: # 1 Exhibit B)\nSealed pursuant to Court Order, ECF 24 .\n(jni) (Entered: 10/17/2023)\n10/19/2023 27 EP: INITIAL APPEARANCE, ARRAIGNMENT AND PLEA TO THE INDICTMENT AND COMPETENCY HEARING held.\n\nDefendant not present, in custody.\n\nInitial Appearance, Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment not held.\n\nDiscussion held and arguments heard regarding competency. Court orders that the Defendant is committed for psychiatric examination pursuant to 18 USC \u00a7 4241and 4247.\n\nThe Court further ORDERS that the proceedings in this case will remain stayed until such time as the above-described hospitalization, treatment and evaluation is completed. The Court finds that period of time from today\nuntil the competency hearing is held be excluded in accordance with 18 U.S.C. 3161(h)1(a) and (h)1(h).\n\nGovernment to prepare order.\n\nStatus conference set for November 17, 2023 at 10:30 a.m. before Magistrate Judge Wes Reber Porter.\nArraignment as to Darren Patrick Riley (1) Count 1, 2 held on 10/19/2023.\nInitial Appearance as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 10/19/2023.\nCompetency Hearing as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 10/19/2023.\nStatus Conference - MJ is set for 11/17/2023 10:30 AM in Courtroom 7 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER.\n\n(FTR-CT 6 / 10:30 - 10:45)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD)\n(jni) (Entered: 10/19/2023)\n10/23/2023 28 ORDER REQUIRING DEFENDANT TO UNDERGO MENTAL EVALUATION AND COMPETENCY EXAMINATION PURSUANT TO 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 4241 AND 4247 as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by\nMAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD on 10/23/2023. (eta) (Entered: 10/23/2023)\n10/25/2023 29 MOTION for Reconsideration re 28 Order for Mental Evaluation Motion to Reconsider Order Requiring Defendant to Undergo Mental Evaluation and Competency Examination Pursuant to 18 U.S.C. Sections 4241 and\n4247 by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration of Counsel, # 2 Certificate of Service)(Yamaga, Melinda) (Entered: 10/25/2023)\n10/30/2023 30 NOTICE OF HEARING ON MOTION in case as to Darren Patrick Riley:\n29 MOTION TO RECONSIDER ORDER REQUIRING DEFENDANT TO UNDERGO MENTAL EVALUATION AND COMPETENCY EXAMINATION PURSUANT TO 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 4241 AND 4247 Hearing is set\nfor 11/08/2023 at 10:00 a.m. in Courtroom 6 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD.\n\n*Government Response is due November 2, 2023.\n\n(bbb) (Entered: 10/30/2023)\n\n11/02/2023 31 RESPONSE to Motion by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley re 29 MOTION for Reconsideration re 28 Order for Mental Evaluation Motion to Reconsider Order Requiring Defendant to Undergo Mental Evaluation and\nCompetency Examination Pursuant to 18 U.S.C. Sections 4241 and 4247 / Certificate of Service (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 11/02/2023)\n11/08/2023 32 Memorandum from FDC Honolulu regarding Defendant Darren Patrick Riley's refusal to be transported by U.S. Marshals Service for court on November 8, 2023. (eta) (Entered: 11/08/2023)\n11/08/2023 33 EP : Motion Hearing re 29 Defendant Darren Patrick Riley's MOTION to Reconsider Order Requiring Defendant to Undergo Mental Evaluation and Competency Examination as to Darren Patrick Riley held on\n11/8/2023.\n\nDefendant not present, in custody. Defendant refused to be transported by the U.S. Marshals Service to attend his scheduled in-person court proceeding 32 .\n\nArguments heard. For the reasons stated on the record, 29 Defendant Darren Patrick Riley's Motion to Reconsider Order Requiring Defendant to Undergo Mental Evaluation and Competency Examination - DENIED.\n\nThe Minutes will stand in place of the order.\n\nIn light of Defendant's assigned transport date of 12/4/2023, the Status conference set for November 17, 2023 at 10:30 a.m. before Magistrate Judge Wes Reber Porter is VACATED.\n\nDefendant to remain in custody at the Federal Detention Center.\n\nMotion Hearing as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 11/8/2023 re 29 MOTION to Reconsider Order Requiring Defendant to Undergo Mental Evaluation filed by Darren Patrick Riley;\ndenying 29 Motion to Reconsider Order Requiring Defendant to Undergo Mental Evaluation filed by Darren Patrick Riley ;\nMotions terminated as to Darren Patrick Riley: 29 MOTION to Reconsider Order Requiring Defendant to Undergo Mental Evaluation filed by Darren Patrick Riley.\n\n(FTR-CT 6 / 10:00-10:10 AM) (MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD)\n(eta) (Entered: 11/08/2023)\n01/04/2024 34 Letter to Magistrate Judge Kenneth J. Mansfield from the U.S. Department of Justice, Federal Bureau of Prisons, Federal Medical Center, Devens, dated December 21, 2023, Re: Defendant Darren Patrick Riley's\nevaluation will be completed by January 17, 2024 with a report to follow within two weeks\n(jo) (Entered: 01/04/2024)\n02/16/2024 36 NOTICE OF HEARING as to Darren Patrick Riley -\n\nA Competency Hearing is set for 02/23/2024 at 9:45 a.m. in Courtroom 6 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD. (bbb) (Entered: 02/16/2024)\n02/20/2024 37 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley -\n\nAt Defendant's counsel request due to a conflict in schedule, the Competency Hearing previously set for 02/23/2024 IS CONTINUED TO 02/27/2024 at 2:00 PM in Courtroom 6 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE\nKENNETH J. MANSFIELD.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD)(bbb) (Entered: 02/20/2024)\n02/22/2024 38 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley -\n\nTo allow sufficient time for Defendant to be transported from FMC Devens in Ayer, MA back to this district, the Competency Hearing previously set for 02/27/2024 IS CONTINUED TO 04/03/2024 at 11:00 a.m. in\nCourtroom 7 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD)(bbb) (Entered: 02/22/2024)\n03/28/2024 39 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley: To allow further time for Defendant's transport to the District of Hawaii, the Competency Hearing set for 4/3/2024 is CONTINUED to 6/21/2024 at 10:30 AM in Courtroom 5 before\nMAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 03/28/2024)\n06/21/2024 40 EP: The following proceedings were held: 1) Competency Hearing as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley; and 2) Arraignment and Plea to the Indictment.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley (\"Defendant\") is present and in custody.\n\nCompetency Hearing:\nCourt is in receipt of the [ECF 35 ] (SEALED) Forensic Report (\"Evaluation\") filed on 2/16/2024. Ms. Yamaga represents Defendant stipulates to the findings concerning Defendant's competency. Neither the Government\nnor the Defendant wish to present other evidence. Parties stipulate Defendant is competent.\nCourt conducts colloquy to confirm Defendant's understanding and agreement to the findings that Defendant is competent to proceed.\n\nBased on the Evaluation and the parties' stipulation, the Court FINDS, by a preponderance of the evidence, that Defendant is COMPETENT and not presently suffering from a major mental disease, disorder, or defect\nwhich impairs his present ability to understand the nature and consequences of the court proceedings against him or to meaningfully assist in his defense.\n\nGovernment to submit competency order to Trader_Orders@hid.uscourts.gov within seven (7) days of this hearing.\n\nProceedings Resumed:\nIn light of the Court having determined Defendant is competent, proceedings are RESUMED.\n\nArraignment and Plea to the Indictment:\nMs. Yamaga represents that [ECF 1 ] Indictment has been received and reviewed with Defendant. Defendant does not waive public reading. Court directs the Government to read the Indictment in its entirety in open\nCourt. Defendant acknowledges understanding the general nature of the charges and pleads not guilty to the Indictment. NOT GUILTY pleas entered.\n\nDates and deadlines are given as follows:\nTrial Dates and Deadlines:\nJury Selection/Jury Trial to follow before Judge Seabright 08/20/2024 at 9:00 AM in Aha Kaulike.\nTrial Conference before Judge Seabright 08/08/2024 at 10:00 AM in Aha Kaulike.\n(See attached Minutes for all dates and deadlines)\n\nDetention Hearing Scheduled:\nAs the Government's [ECF 5 ] Motion to Detain Defendant Without Bail, filed 8/25/2023 has not yet been heard, the Court schedules a detention hearing for 6/26/24 at 10:30 a.m. before Magistrate Judge Trader in\nCourtroom 5.\n\nDue Process Protection Act Advisory:\nThe Court orders the United States to comply with its disclosure obligations under Brady v. Maryland and its progeny. Failing to timely do so may result in consequences to include sanctions, adverse jury instructions,\nexclusion of evidence, and dismissal of charges. This order incorporates the provisions of the Court's February 1, 2021 General Order Regarding Rule 5(F).\n\nSpeedy Trial Act Exclusions:\nPursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a73161(h)(1)(A), the Court FINDS the time period from 10/19/2023 (Court orally orders competency evaluation) up to and including 6/21/2024 (Defendant's competency determined), shall be\nEXCLUDED pursuant to the Speedy Trial Act. Ms. Yamaga reserves the right to challenge the Court's findings that the foregoing time period is excludable.\n\nDefendant is remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nCompetency Hearing as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 6/21/2024.\nArraignment as to Darren Patrick Riley (1) Counts 1, 2 held on 6/21/2024.\nDetention Hearing is set for 6/26/2024 10:30 AM in Courtroom 5 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER.\nJury Selection/Trial is set for 09:00 AM on 8/20/2024 in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nTrial Conference is set for 8/8/2024 10:00 AM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(FTR-CT 5 / 11:03 AM-11:22 AM)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER)\n(jni) (Entered: 06/21/2024)\n\n06/21/2024 41 CRIMINAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 6/21/2024.\n(jni) (Entered: 06/21/2024)\n06/25/2024 42 EO: as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley - An Initial Pretrial Conference is set for 07/05/2024 at 01:30 PM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 06/25/2024)\n06/25/2024 43 ORDER FINDING DEFENDANT MENTALLY COMPETENT TO STAND TRIAL as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 6/25/2024.\n(jni) (Entered: 06/25/2024)\n06/26/2024 44 EP: DETENTION HEARING as to DEFENDANT DARREN PATRICK RILEY held on 06/26/2024.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley (\"Defendant\") present and in custody.\n\nCourt takes judicial notice of its records and files, including the Government's [ECF 5 ] Motion to Detain Defendant Without Bail (\"Motion\"), the report and recommendation of Pretrial Services and applicable legal\nauthority.\n\nArgument had.\n\nCourt has carefully considered the merits of the Government's Motion within the context of the arguments by counsel and the report by Pretrial Services and finds that there are no conditions adequate to reasonably ensure\nDefendant's presence and to mitigate any risk of danger posed by Defendant if released. Court further finds that the defense has failed to rebut the presumption in favor of detention.\nGovernment's [ECF 5 ] Motion to Detain Defendant Without Bail is GRANTED.\n\nThese minutes will stand in place of a written order.\n\nDefendant is remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshal Service.\nDetention Hearing as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 6/26/2024.\nGranting 5 Motion to Detain as to Darren Patrick Riley (1).\n\n(FTR-CT 5 / 10:42 am 11:03 am)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER)\n(jni) (Entered: 06/26/2024)\n07/05/2024 45 EP: INITIAL PRETRIAL CONFERENCE\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, not present.\n\nMs. Neha Khan, FDC Staff Attorney, participated by telephone.\n\nDiscussion held regarding (1) Defendant's refusal to be transported from FDC Honolulu to the courthouse, and (2) the August 20, 2024 trial date.\n\nMs. Khan told the Court what occurred this morning that resulted in Defendant's failure to appear for this hearing. Further Initial Pretrial Conference is set for July 9, 2024 at 9:00 a.m. in Aha Kaulike before the Honorable\nJ. Michael Seabright. Ms. Khan asked whether the U.S. Marshals Service could use reasonable force if Defendant refuses to be transported to the courthouse - For reasons stated on the record, no force will be used. The\nCourt will vacate and not rely on Order to Produce, ECF No. 16.\n\nMs. Yamaga stated that Defendant has not yet received any discovery. Government indicated that the delay is due to the nature of the discovery in this case, and that it will continue to work on getting discovery to\nDefendant.\n\nMs. Yamaga will meet with Defendant this afternoon.\nStatus Conference - DJ as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 7/5/2024.\nFurther Status Conference - DJ is set for 7/9/2024 09:00 AM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(Reporter-Ann Matsumoto)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 07/05/2024)\n07/09/2024 46 EP: FURTHER INITIAL PRETRIAL CONFERENCE\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, present.\n\nDiscussion held regarding current trial date.\n\nMs. Yamaga stated that there is still outstanding discovery; however, Defendant would like to proceed with Jury Selection/Trial on August 20, 2024.\n\nCounsel given a copy of the current Jury Questionnaire for Federal Jury Service (\"Questionnaire\") to review. Parties had no objection to the Questionnaire. Defendant will file his objection, if any, after further review. The\nCourt informed Counsel that it will make decisions on requests to be excused from jury service.\n\nThe Court will issue a Criminal Scheduling Order.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nStatus Conference - DJ as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 7/9/2024.\n\n(Reporter-Ann Matsumoto)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 07/09/2024)\n07/09/2024 47 MOTION to Compel Motion to Compel Discovery or, in the Alternative, to Exclude Search Warrant Evidence by Darren Patrick Riley. (Yamaga, Melinda) (Entered: 07/09/2024)\n07/09/2024 48 MOTION to Dismiss on Speedy Trial Defendant's Motion to Dismiss by Darren Patrick Riley. (Yamaga, Melinda) (Entered: 07/09/2024)\n07/09/2024 49 EO: On July 9, 2024, Defendant Darren Patrick Riley filed a: (1) Motion to Compel Discovery or, in the Alternative, to Exclude Search Warrant Evidence, ECF No. 47 (\"Motion to Compel\"); and (2) Motion to Dismiss\nunder the Speedy Trial Act, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3161 et seq., ECF No. 48 (\"Motion to Dismiss\").\n\nA hearing on the Motion to Compel is set for July 16, 2024, at 1:30 p.m. in Aha Kaulike. The government's response is due by July 12, 2024.\n\nA hearing on the Motion to Dismiss is set for July 19, 2024, at 10:00 a.m. in Aha Nonoi. The government's response is due by July 16, 2024.\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/09/2024)\n\n07/10/2024 50 EO: in case as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley - Due a conflict in the court's calendar, Defendant's Motion to Compel Discovery (ECF No. 47 ) set for 07/16/2024 at 1:30 PM is continued to 3:00 PM on the same day in\nAha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/10/2024)\n07/10/2024 51 CRIMINAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT on 7/10/2024.\n(jni) (Entered: 07/10/2024)\n07/10/2024 52 NOTICE Withdrawal of Motion to Compel Discovery or, in the Alternative, to Exclude Search Warrant Evidence by Darren Patrick Riley re 47 MOTION to Compel Motion to Compel Discovery or, in the Alternative, to\nExclude Search Warrant Evidence (Yamaga, Melinda) (Entered: 07/10/2024)\n07/11/2024 53 EO: On July 10, 2024, Defendant filed a Withdrawal of Motion to Compel Discovery or, in the Alternative, to Exclude Search Warrant Evidence, ECF No. 52 . Therefore, government's July 12, 2024 response deadline and\nthe hearing on the motion set for July 16, 2024 are VACATED.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/11/2024)\n07/12/2024 54 EO: Hearing on 48 Motion to Dismiss set for July 19, 2024 at 10:00 AM will be held in Aha Kanawai.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/12/2024)\n07/12/2024 55 MOTION for Protective Order Motion for Stipulated Protective Order Limiting the Disclosure of Discovery Materials/COS by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 07/12/2024)\n07/15/2024 56 MOTION to Continue Motion to Continue Trial and Continue Hearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss by Darren Patrick Riley. (Yamaga, Melinda) (Entered: 07/15/2024)\n07/15/2024 57 EO: in case as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley - Motion to Continue Trial and Continue Hearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss, ECF No. 56 , is set for July 16, 2024 at 10:30 AM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J.\nMICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/15/2024)\n07/15/2024 58 EO: On September 28, 2023, Magistrate Judge Wes Reber Porter entered an Order to Produce that authorized the United States Marshals Service to bring Defendant Darren Patrick Riley to court, \"even if the use of\nreasonable force is necessary.\" ECF. No. 16 . The court rescinds the authorization of using reasonable force given Defendant's recent willingness to appear in court. Should Defendant again refuse to leave the Federal\nDetention Center for court appearances, the court will revisit the issue of a reasonable use of force order.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/15/2024)\n07/15/2024 59 EO: On July 15, 2024, counsel for Defendant Darren Patrick Riley (\"Defendant\") filed a Motion to Continue Trial and Continue Hearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss (\"Motion\"), ECF No. 56 . The Motion seeks a\ncontinuance of the trial date, even though Defendant \"does not agree with counsel's request.\" Id. at PageID.283. The court thus construes the Motion as being brought by defense counsel over Defendant's objection.\n\nThe Motion, however, contains no discussion of the law, and specifically no case law on whether the court has the authority--when requested by defense counsel-- to: 1) continue a trial over a defendant's objection; and 2)\ntoll time under the Speedy Trial Act over a defendant's objection. Courts have found no Speedy Trial Act violation where counsel sought a continuance without consulting with a criminal defendant and obtaining his\nconsent beforehand. See, e.g., United States v. Robinson, 67 F.4th 742, 74849 (5th Cir. 2023). Here, however, the defendant has affirmatively objected.\n\nThe court also understands that defense counsel sought an expedited hearing on the Motion, which the court granted, setting the Motion for hearing on July 16, 2024. ECF No. 57 . Thus, counsel for Defendant is required\nto provide the court, by midnight tonight (July 15, 2024), case law that addresses these questions. Counsel for the government may, but is not required, to do the same.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/15/2024)\n07/15/2024 60 Supplement Clarification and Caselaw Regarding Motion to Continue Trial re 56 MOTION to Continue Motion to Continue Trial and Continue Hearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss, 59 Link,,,,,, by Darren Patrick\nRiley (Yamaga, Melinda) (Entered: 07/15/2024)\n07/16/2024 61 EP: MOTION TO CONTINUE TRIAL AND CONTINUE HEARING ON DEFENDANT'S MOTION TO DISMISS\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, present.\n\nDiscussion held and oral arguments heard.\n\nThe Court conducted colloquy with Defendant regarding him addressing the Court directly. Defendant addressed the Court.\n\n56 Motion to Continue Trial and Continue Hearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss - For reasons stated on the record, GRANTED.\n\nJury Selection/Trial is continued from August 20, 2024 to November 5, 2024. Motions, other than motions in limine or motions based on expert witness disclosures, are due by September 30, 2024. Responses are due by\nOctober 11, 2024.\n\nThe Court directed the Government to prepare and submit an Order granting the motion to continue trial by July 19, 2024.\n\nDates and deadlines set forth in Criminal Scheduling Order, ECF No. 51, are VACATED.\nHearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss, ECF No. 48, is continued from July 19, 2024 to July 25, 2024 at 2:00 p.m. in Aha Kaulike before the Honorable J. Michael Seabright.\n\nGovernment's response is now due on July 19, 2024. Defendant's reply is due July 22, 2024.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nMotion Hearing as to Darren Patrick Riley re 56 Motion to Continue Trial and Continue Hearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss filed by Darren Patrick Riley, held on 7/16/2024.\nGranting 56 Motion to Continue as to Darren Patrick Riley (1).\nHearing re 48 Defendant's Motion to Dismiss filed by Darren Patrick Riley CONTINUED to 7/25/2024 02:00 PM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nJury Selection/Trial is CONTINUED to 09:00 AM on 11/5/2024 in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(Reporter-Ann Matsumoto)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 07/16/2024)\n\n07/17/2024 62 STIPULATED PROTECTIVE ORDER LIMITING THE DISCLOSURE OF DISCOVERY MATERIALS re 55 as to Darren Patrick Riley (1) - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER on 7/17/2024.\n(jni) (Entered: 07/17/2024)\n07/17/2024 63 RESPONSE by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley re 48 MOTION to Dismiss on Speedy Trial Defendant's Motion to Dismiss Government's Response to Defendant's Motion to Dismiss on Speedy Trial Grounds/COS\n(Attachments: # 1 Exhibit A, # 2 Exhibit B, # 3 Exhibit C)(Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 07/17/2024)\n07/18/2024 64 ORDER CONTINUING TRIAL DATE AND EXCLUDING TIME UNDER THE SPEEDY TRIAL ACT as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT on 7/18/2024.\n(1) Jury selection and trial are set for November 5, 2024 at 9:00 a.m.;\n(2) Expert witness disclosures are due as required by this Court's April 21, 2023 General Order Regarding Fed. R. Crim. P. 16(a)(1)(G)(ii) and 16(b)(1)(C)(ii);\n(3) Pretrial Conference before Hon. J. Michael Seabright is set for September 17, 2024 at 10:00 a.m.;\n(4) Motions deadline is set for September 30, 2024; and the\n(5) Response deadline is set for October 11, 2024.\n\nPretrial Conference is set for 9/17/2024 10:00 AM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n***Time Excluded as to Darren Patrick Riley: (7/16/2024-11/5/2024)\n(jni) (Entered: 07/18/2024)\n07/22/2024 65 TRANSCRIPT of Proceedings as to Darren Patrick Riley - held on 9/29/2023, before Judge Wes Reber Porter. Court Reporter/Transcriber - Jessica Cahill, Telephone number -(808)298-8633.Email Address -\nmaukele@hawaii.rr.com, PP. 17, 90-Day Transcript Restriction: PACER access to filed transcripts is restricted for 90 days from the file date to permit redaction of personal identifiers. Citations to restricted transcripts in\nfiled documents must be limited to those portions of the proceedings that are relevant and in need of judicial review. Attaching restricted transcripts, in their entirety, to filed documents should be limited to situations with\nspecific need. Transcript may be viewed at the court public terminal or ordered through the Court Reporter before the deadline for Release of Transcript. Redaction Request due 8/12/2024. Redacted Transcript Deadline set\nfor 8/22/2024. Release of Transcript Restriction set for 10/21/2024. (Cahill, Jesscia) (Entered: 07/22/2024)\n07/22/2024 66 REPLY by Darren Patrick Riley re 63 Response, Defendant's Reply to the Government's Response (ECF 63) to his Motion to Dismiss (ECF 48) (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit A, # 2 Certificate of Service)(Yamaga, Melinda)\n(Entered: 07/22/2024)\n07/22/2024 67 EO: In preparation for the July 25, 2024 hearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss based on the Speedy Trial Act, ECF No. 48 , counsel should be prepared to discuss the impact of the Government's Motion to Detain\nWithout Bail, ECF No. 5 , on the Speedy Trial clock. Here, the Government's motion to detain was filed on August 25, 2023 and a hearing was held on June 6, 2024, when the motion was granted. ECF No. 44 . Is the time\nperiod from August 25, 2023 through June 6, 2024 tolled pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 3161(h)(1)(D)? Counsel should review, at a minimum, the following cases: Henderson v. United States, 476 U.S. 321 (1986); United States\nv. Medina, 524 F.3d 974 (9th Cir. 2008); and United States v. Beler, 2019 WL 5789747 (D.D.C. Nov. 6, 2019).\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/22/2024)\n07/25/2024 68 NOTICE Notice of Supplemental Authority by Darren Patrick Riley re 66 Reply, Reply to Response (Yamaga, Melinda) (Entered: 07/25/2024)\n07/25/2024 69 EO: In preparation for the July 25, 2024 hearing on Defendant's Motion to Dismiss based on the Speedy Trial Act, ECF No. 48 , counsel should prepared to discuss whether United States v. Lewis, 349 F.3d 1116 (9th Cir.\n2003) (cited in Defendant's Notice of Supplemental Authority, ECF No. 68 ) was overruled by United States v. Tinklenberg, 563 U.S. 647 (2011).\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/25/2024)\n07/25/2024 70 SUPERSEDING INDICTMENT as to Darren Patrick Riley (1) count(s) 1s, 2s, 3s, 4s, 5s, 6s, 7s, 8s, 9s, 10s, 11s, 12s.\n(jni) (Entered: 07/25/2024)\n07/25/2024 72 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley - An Arraignment to the Superseding Indictment is set for 7/25/2024 at 02:00 PM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jo) (Entered: 07/25/2024)\n07/25/2024 74 EP: ARRAIGNMENT AND PLEA TO THE SUPERCEDING INDICTMENT; DEFENDANT'S MOTION TO DISMISS\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, present.\n\nArraignment and Plea to the Superceding Indictment:\nMs. Yamaga represents that Superceding Indictment (ECF No. 70) has been received and reviewed with Defendant. Defendant waives public reading. Defendant acknowledges understanding the general nature of the\ncharges and pleads not guilty to the Superceding Indictment. NOT GUILTY pleas entered.\n\nJury Selection/Trial remains set for November 5, 2024. Dates/Deadlines also remain as set forth in the Criminal Scheduling Order, ECF No. 51.\n\nThe Court advised the government of its obligation to produce all exculpatory evidence to the defendant pursuant to Brady v. Maryland, 373 U.S. 83 (1963) and its progeny, and orders it to do so. Failing to do so in a\ntimely manner may result in consequences, including exclusion of evidence, adverse jury instructions, dismissal of charges, contempt proceedings, or sanctions by the Court.\n\nDefendant's Motion to Dismiss:\nDiscussion held and oral arguments heard.\n\n48 Defendant's Motion to Dismiss - For reasons stated on the record, DENIED.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nArraignment as to Darren Patrick Riley (1) Count 1s, 2s, 3s, 4s, 5s, 6s, 7s, 8s, 9s, 10s, 11s, 12s held on 7/25/2024.\nMotion Hearing re 48 Defendant's Motion to Dismiss filed by Darren Patrick Riley held on 7/25/2024.\nDenying 48 Motion to Dismiss for Speedy Trial as to Darren Patrick Riley (1).\n\n(Reporter-Ann Matsumoto)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 07/25/2024)\n07/25/2024 81 AMENDED EP: ARRAIGNMENT AND PLEA TO THE SUPERCEDING INDICTMENT; DEFENDANT'S MOTION TO DISMISS\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, present.\n\nArraignment and Plea to the Superceding Indictment:\nMs. Yamaga represents that Superceding Indictment (ECF No. 70) has been received and reviewed with Defendant. Defendant waives public reading. Defendant acknowledges understanding the general nature of the\ncharges and pleads not guilty to the Superceding Indictment. NOT GUILTY pleas entered.\n\nJury Selection/Trial remains set for November 5, 2024.\n\nThe Court advised the government of its obligation to produce all exculpatory evidence to the defendant pursuant to Brady v. Maryland, 373 U.S. 83 (1963) and its progeny, and orders it to do so. Failing to do so in a\ntimely manner may result in consequences, including exclusion of evidence, adverse jury instructions, dismissal of charges, contempt proceedings, or sanctions by the Court.\n\nDefendant's Motion to Dismiss:\nDiscussion held and oral arguments heard.\n\n48 Defendant's Motion to Dismiss - For reasons stated on the record, DENIED.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\n\n(Reporter-Ann Matsumoto)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 08/12/2024)\n07/26/2024 75 ORDER DENYING MOTION TO DISMISS BASED ON THE SPEEDY TRIAL ACT, ECF NO. 48 as to Darren Patrick Riley re 48 - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT on 7/26/2024.\n(jni) (Entered: 07/26/2024)\n07/26/2024 76 Summons Returned Executed on 7/25/2024 as to Darren Patrick Riley.\n(jni) (Entered: 07/26/2024)\n07/28/2024 77 MOTION to Continue Trial and to Declare Case Complex by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 07/28/2024)\n07/29/2024 78 NOTICE OF HEARING ON MOTION as to Darren Patrick Riley - A hearing on ECF No. 77 MOTION to Declare Case Complex and to Continue Trial is set for 8/9/2024 at 10:00 AM in Courtroom 6 before\nMAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD. Defendant's response is due 8/6/2024.\n\nParties are directed to review Rule 10.3 of the Local Rules of Practice for the United States District Court for the District of Hawaii regarding requirements for Mandatory Chambers Copies.\n\n(jo)\nDocket Text Modified on 7/29/2024 (jo)\n\n(Entered: 07/29/2024)\n07/31/2024 79 EO: in case as to Darren Patrick Riley - By agreement of the parties, the hearing on 77 MOTION to Continue Trial and to Declare Case Complex previously set for 8/9/2024 at 10:00 am is ADVANCED to 8/8/2024 at\n10:00 am in Courtroom 6 before Magistrate Judge Kenneth J. Mansfield.\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)(sj) (Entered: 07/31/2024)\n08/08/2024 80 EP: 77 MOTION TO DECLARE CASE COMPLEX AND TO CONTINUE TRIAL hearing held.\n\nDefendant is present and in custody.\n\nArguments heard.\n\n77 Motion to Declare Case Complex and to Continue Trial is DENIED.\n\nCourt to prepare the order.\nMotion Hearing re 77 MOTION to Continue Trial and to Declare Case Complex filed by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 8/8/2024.\nDenying 77 Motion to Continue as to Darren Patrick Riley (1).\n\n(FTR-CT 6 / 10:00 - 10:26)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD)\n(jni) (Entered: 08/08/2024)\n08/08/2024 84 AMENDED EP: 77 MOTION TO DECLARE CASE COMPLEX AND TO CONTINUE TRIAL hearing held.\n\nDefendant is present and in custody.\n\nArguments heard.\n\n77 Motion to Declare Case Complex and to Continue Trial is DENIED.\n\nThe Court's oral ruling will stand in place of a written order.\n\n(FTR-CT 6 / 10:0010:26)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE KENNETH J. MANSFIELD)\n(jni) (Entered: 08/29/2024)\n08/28/2024 82 ORDER REASSIGNING CASE as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by CHIEF JUDGE DERRICK K. WATSON on 8/28/2024. Please reflect new Criminal case number CR 23-00071 JAO.\n(jni) (Entered: 08/28/2024)\n08/29/2024 83 EO: The parties are directed to review the General Criminal Case Procedures Before Judge Otake posted on the court's website and are expected to comply with the most recent version that is posted.\n\n(JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE)(shm) (Entered: 08/29/2024)\n08/29/2024 85 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley, a Status Conference is SET for 9/4/2024 at 10:00 AM in Aha Kanawai before JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE.\n\nThe Court intends to address the following at the status conference:\n(1) Filing deadlines\n(2) Anticipated motions\n(3) Potential jury questionnaires\n(4) Suggestions on handling contraband in the course of the trial\n(5) Trial schedule\n\n(JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE)(shm) (Entered: 08/29/2024)\n09/04/2024 86 EP: Status Conference as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley was held.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley was not present.\n\nUSMS Angelique Kahao-Poe informs the Court that Defendant was not feeling well at the FDC this morning and so was not transported. It did not appear to her that he was refusing to attend the hearing.\n\nDiscussion held regarding the 11/5/2024 trial date, proposed jury questionnaires, current motions deadlines, and expert disclosures.\n\nI. Filing Deadlines\n\nParties represent that they agree to a one-week continuance of the expert disclosures. Parties to submit the stipulation to Judge Otake's orders box by 9/6/2024.\n\nII. Anticipated Motions\nMs. Yamaga intends to file additional motions.\n\nMs. Perlmutter may file a motion to continue the trial if defense motions are filed and may supersede the Indictment. Ms. Yamaga adds that the defense may file a motion to continue the trial.\n\nIII. Potential Jury Questionnaires\n\nThe Court will file a proposed questionnaire. Parties' objections to the proposed questionnaire are due by 9/18/2024. Ms. Yamaga may also state in her filing her position on whether the questionnaires should be issued\nbefore jury selection or the morning of jury selection.\n\nIV. Suggestions on Handling Contraband in the Course of the Trial\n\nParties to meet and confer to discuss how trial evidence will be published to the jury.\n\nV. Trial Schedule\n\nJury Selection/Jury Trial is ADVANCED to 11/4/2024 at 9:00 AM in Aha Kanawai. An Amended Criminal Scheduling Order will be issued. Trial will not be conducted on 11/7/2024 and 11/8/2024.\n\n(Reporter-Beth Krupa)\n(JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE)(shm) (Entered: 09/04/2024)\n09/04/2024 87 EO: REVISED DATES AND DEADLINES FOR AN AMENDED CRIMINAL SCHEDULING ORDER RE: NOVEMBER 4, 2024 TRIAL DATE\n\nPursuant to discussion held during the September 4, 2024 Status Conference, new trial date and trial related deadlines are set forth below.\n\nCourt to issue an Amended Criminal Scheduling Order.\n\nJury Selection/Trial is SET for 11/4/2024 at 9:00 AM in Aha Kanawai before DISTRICT JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE.\nTrial Conference is SET for 10/21/2024 at 9:00 AM before DISTRICT JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE.\nJoint Trial Presentation Statement is SET for 10/17/2024.\nMotions Deadline is SET for 9/30/2024.\nResponses Deadline is SET for 10/11/2024.\nFed. R. Evid. 404(b) is SET for 9/30/2024.\n\n(JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE)(shm) (Entered: 09/04/2024)\n09/04/2024 88 AMENDED CRIMINAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE on 9/4/2024.\nTrial Conference is set for 10/21/2024 09:00 AM in Aha Kanawai before JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE.\n(jni) (Entered: 09/04/2024)\n09/05/2024 89 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney Motion for Withdrawal and Substitution of Counsel by Melinda K. Yamaga. by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration of Counsel, # 2 Certificate of Service)(Yamaga,\nMelinda) (Entered: 09/05/2024)\n09/05/2024 90 PROPOSED SPECIAL QUESTIONNAIRE as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE on 9/5/2024.\n(jni) (Entered: 09/05/2024)\n09/05/2024 91 NOTICE OF HEARING ON MOTION as to Darren Patrick Riley - A hearing on ECF No. 89 Motion for Withdrawal and Substitution of Counsel is set for 9/11/2024 at 9:30 AM in Courtroom 5 before MAGISTRATE\nJUDGE ROM TRADER.\n(ab) (Entered: 09/05/2024)\n09/05/2024 92 EO: In light of 89 Motion for Withdrawal and Substitution of Counsel (\"Motion\") filed by AFPD Yamaga, the Court VACATES the deadline for the filing of a stipulation to extend the expert disclosure deadline. See ECF\nNo. 86. The Court also VACATES the current deadlines in paragraph 10 of the 88 Amended Criminal Scheduling Order. The Court will reset the deadlines after the hearing on the Motion.\n\n(JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE)(shm) (Entered: 09/05/2024)\n09/05/2024 93 EO: as to Darren Patrick Riley - At the request of the parties, the hearing on ECF No. 89 Motion for Withdrawal and Substitution of Counsel set for 9/11/2024 is ADVANCED to 9/6/2024 at 02:00 PM in Courtroom 5\nbefore MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER)\n(jo) (Entered: 09/05/2024)\n09/06/2024 94 EP: MOTION HEARING regarding Defendant's [ECF 89 ] Motion for Withdrawal and Substitution of Counsel (\"Motion\") had on 9/6/2024.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley (\"Defendant\") present and in custody.\n\nCourt takes judicial notice of its records and files, including the [ECF 1 ] Indictment, the instant Motion, and prior proceedings.\nCourt moves to closed hearing.\n\nSEALED HEARING: (2:03 p.m. 2:17 p.m.)\n\nCourt made inquiries of Defendant and Ms. Yamaga.\n\nProceeding re-opened: (2:18 p.m. 2:22 p.m.)\n\nMs. Perlmutter returns to the courtroom.\n\nBased upon an irreparable breakdown in communication and the attorney-client relationship, the Court finds good cause and GRANTS the Motion. Ms. Yamaga is permitted to withdraw as counsel. Substitute CJA counsel\nto be appointed.\n\nMs. Yamaga to prepare and submit order to the Court's orders box at Trader_Orders@hid.uscourts.gov within seven (7) days of this hearing.\n\nGovernment informs the Court of no known conflicts with respect to CJA panel attorneys.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nMotion Hearing as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 9/6/2024 re 89 Motion for Withdrawal and Substitution of Counsel\n89 Motion for Withdrawal and Substitution of Counsel: Granted\n\n(FTR-CT 5 / 2:01 pm - 2:22 pm (Sealed: 2:03 - 2:17 pm))\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER)\n(jo) (Entered: 09/06/2024)\n09/09/2024 95 CJA 20 as to Darren Patrick Riley: Harlan Y. Kimura, Esq. appointed - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 9/9/2024.\nSubstitution for Melinda K. Yamaga, AFPD\nNunc Pro Tunc: 9/6/2024\n(jni) (Entered: 09/09/2024)\n09/09/2024 96 ORDER GRANTING MOTION FOR WITHDRAWAL AND SUBSTITUTION OF COUNSEL as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 9/9/2024.\n(jni) (Entered: 09/09/2024)\n09/11/2024 97 EO: as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley, a Status Conference is SET for 9/17/2024 at 2:00 PM in Aha Kanawai before JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE. Defendant must attend the hearing in-person.\n\n(JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE)(shm) (Entered: 09/11/2024)\n09/17/2024 98 EP: Status Conference as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley was held.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley was present, in custody.\n\nMr. Kimura requests a sealed hearing.\n\n(2:10pm - AUSA Rebecca Perlmutter is excused from the courtroom; Court seals courtroom).\n\nSealed discussion held between Defendant, defense counsel and the Court. Court conducted a colloquy with Defendant.\n\n(2:13pm- AUSA Rebecca Perlmutter returns)\n\nMr. Kimura to file a Motion to Continue Trial.\n\nParties' deadline to file an objection to the 90 Proposed Special Questionnaire set for 9/18/2024 is hereby VACATED.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley is remanded into the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\n\n(Reporter-Cynthia Fazio)\n(JUDGE JILL A. OTAKE)(shm) (Entered: 09/17/2024)\n09/17/2024 99 Defendant Darren Patrick Riley's Unopposed MOTION to Continue Trial Date and Related Deadlines by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration Of Counsel, # 2 Certificate of Service)(Kimura, Harlan)\nModified on 9/18/2024 (jni) (Entered: 09/17/2024)\n\n09/18/2024 100 NOTICE OF HEARING ON MOTION as to Darren Patrick Riley - A hearing on ECF No. 99 Defendant Darren Patrick Rileys Unopposed Motion to Continue Trial Date and Related Deadlines is set for 9/20/2024 at 9:30\na.m. in Courtroom 5 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER.\n(ab) (Entered: 09/18/2024)\n09/20/2024 101 EP: MOTION HEARING regarding Defendant's [ECF 99 ] Unopposed Motion to Continue Trial Date and Related Deadlines (\"Unopposed Motion\") as to DEFENDANT DARREN PATRICK RILEY had on 9/20/2024.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley (\"Defendant\") not present. Court provides counsel with information concerning Defendant's absence. U.S. Marshals Service reports that Defendant declined transport to Court base upon\nmedical reasons. Court finds Defendant's absence is excusable. At request of Mr. Kimura, Court waives Defendant's presence for the purposes of today's proceeding only.\n\nMr. Kimura reports that Defendant affirmatively consents to a trial continuance in this case. Moreover, Mr. Kimura represents that Defendant recently appeared before District Judge Otake and consented on-the-record to a\ncontinuance of his trial. ECF No. 98.\n\nCourt takes judicial notice of its records and files, including all prior proceedings.\n\nUnopposed Motion:\n\nBased upon the Court's finding of good cause, the Unopposed Motion is GRANTED. Trial is CONTINUED from 11/5/2024 to 4/29/2025 before District Judge J. Michael Seabright. Deadlines adjusted consistent with the\nnew trial date. These minutes shall stand in place of a written order granting the Unopposed Motion.\n\nSecond Amended Criminal Scheduling Order to issue.\n\nTrial Dates and Deadlines:\n\nJury Selection/Jury Trial to follow on 04/29/2025 at 9:00 AM before Judge J. Michael Seabright.\nTrial Conference on 04/17/2025 at 9:00 AM before Judge J. Michael Seabright.\n\n(Please see attached Minutes for all trial dates and deadlines)\n\nSpeedy Trial Exclusions:\n\nThe Court finds that the ends of justice served by the continuance outweigh the best interests of the defendant and the public in a speedy trial, and that the failure to grant a continuance from 11/4/2024 to 4/29/2025 would\nlikely result in a miscarriage of justice.\n\nIn evaluating whether to grant such continuance, the Court considered various factors including the following: 1) that Defendant consents to the continuance; 2) that the existing 11/4/2024 trial is only six (6) weeks away;\n3) that new counsel (Mr. Kimura) wasappointed on 9/9/2024; 4) that the nature, extent and volume of discovery in this case will require substantial time to review; 5) that while this case has not been designated complex,\nboth the Government and defense intend to retain numerous experts for trial;and 6) that given the nature of this case, Mr. Kimura intends to request the Court appoint associate counsel in this matter.\n\nThe Court has determined that the foregoing factors support a finding that the ends of justice served by granting a continuance outweigh the best interests of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial. Furthermore, the\nCourt finds that the failure to grant the requested continuance would deny counsel for the defendant the reasonable time necessary for effective preparation, taking into account the exercise of due diligence.\n\nThe Court finds the period of time from 9/17/2024 (the filing of the instant Unopposed Motion) to the new trial date of 4/29/2025, constitutes a period of delay which shall be EXCLUDED in computing the time within\nwhich the trial in this case must commence pursuant to the Speedy Trial Act, 18 U.S.C. Sections 3161(h)(1)(D), (h)(7)(A), and (h)(7)(B)(i) & (iv).\nMotion Hearing re 99 MOTION to Continue Trial Date and Related Deadlines filed by Darren Patrick Riley held on 9/20/2024.\nGranting 99 Motion to Continue as to Darren Patrick Riley (1).\nJury Selection/Trial is set for 09:00 AM on 4/29/2025 before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nTrial Conference is set for 4/17/2025 09:00 AM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n***Time Excluded as to Darren Patrick Riley: (9/17/2024-4/29/2025)\n\n(FTR-CT 5 / 9:29 AM - 9:40 AM)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER)\n(jni) (Entered: 09/20/2024)\n09/20/2024 102 SECOND AMENDED CRIMINAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 9/20/2024.\n(jni) (Entered: 09/20/2024)\n09/24/2024 103 ORDER REASSIGNING CASE as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by CHIEF JUDGE DERRICK K. WATSON on 9/24/2024. Please reflect new Criminal case number CR 23-00071 JMS on all further pleadings.\n(jni) (Entered: 09/24/2024)\n01/10/2025 104 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney For Defendant by Harlan Y. Kimura. by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration Of Counsel, # 2 Certificate of Service)(Kimura, Harlan) (Entered: 01/10/2025)\n01/13/2025 105 NOTICE OF HEARING ON MOTION as to Darren Patrick Riley - A hearing on ECF No. 104 Motion to Withdraw as Counsel for Defendant is set for 1/14/2025 at 10:00 AM in Courtroom 5 before MAGISTRATE\nJUDGE ROM TRADER.\n(ab) (Entered: 01/13/2025)\n01/14/2025 106 EP: MOTION HEARING regarding Defendant's [ECF 104 ] Motion to Withdraw as Counsel for Defendant (\"Motion\") as to DEFENDANT Darren Patrick Riley had on 1/14/2025.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley (\"Defendant\") present and in custody.\n\nCourt takes judicial notice of its records and files, including all prior proceedings.\nCourt moves to closed hearing.\n\nSEALED HEARING: (10:04 a.m. 10:08 a.m.)\n\nCourt made inquiries of Defendant and Mr. Kimura.\n\nProceeding re-opened: (10:08 a.m. 10:11 a.m.)\n\nMs. Perlmutter returns to the courtroom.\n\nBased upon a breakdown in the attorney-client relationship, the Court finds good cause and GRANTS the Motion. Mr. Kimura is permitted to withdraw as counsel. Substitute CJA counsel to be appointed.\n\nGovernment reports no known conflicts preventing any CJA counsel from representing Defendant.\n\nThese minutes will stand in place of a separate written order.\nMotion Hearing re 104 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Harlan Y. Kimura as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 1/14/2025.\nGranting 104 Motion to Withdraw as Attorney as to Darren Patrick Riley (1).\n\n(FTR-CT CT 5 / 10:00 AM - 10:11 AM)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER)\n(jni) (Entered: 01/14/2025)\n01/14/2025 107 CJA 20 as to Darren Patrick Riley: Appointment of G. Gary Singh, Esq. - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 1/14/2025.\nSubs for Panel Attorney Harlan Y. Kimura\n(jni) (Entered: 01/14/2025)\n01/21/2025 108 MOTION to Continue Trial Date by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration of Counsel, # 2 Certificate of Service)(Singh, Gary) (Entered: 01/21/2025)\n01/21/2025 111 NOTICE OF HEARING ON MOTION - as to Darren Patrick Riley - A hearing on ECF No. 108 Motion to Continue Trial Date is set for 1/23/2025 at 10:30 AM in Courtroom 5 before MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM\nTRADER.\n(ab) (Entered: 01/21/2025)\n01/23/2025 112 EP: MOTION HEARING regarding Defendant's [ECF 108 ] Defendant's Motion to Continue Trial Date (\"Motion\") as to DEFENDANT DARREN PATRICK RILEY had on 1/23/2025.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley (\"Defendant\") present and in custody.\n\nDiscussion had.\n\nCourt takes judicial notice of its records and files, including all prior proceedings.\n\nBased upon the Court's finding of good cause, the Motion is GRANTED. Trial is CONTINUED from 4/29/2025 to 9/30/2025 before Senior District Judge Seabright. Deadlines adjusted consistent with the new trial date.\n\nThird Amended Criminal Scheduling Order to issue.\n\nTrial Dates and Deadlines:\n\nJury Selection/Jury Trial to follow on 09/30/2025 at 9:00 AM before Judge J. Michael Seabright.\nTrial Conference on 09/18/2025 at 10:00 AM before Judge J. Michael Seabright.\n\nSpeedy Trial Exclusion:\n\nThe Court finds the ends of justice served by the continuance outweigh the best interests of the defendant and the public in a speedy trial, and that the failure to grant a continuance from 4/29/2025 to 9/30/2025 would\nlikely result in a miscarriage of justice. In granting such continuance, the Court considered various factors including the following: Mr. Singh's recent appointment, Defendant's consent, nature and severity of the charged\noffenses, the nature and extent of discovery, and the need for reasonable time to evaluate defenses, pretrial motions and to prepare for trial.\n\nThe Court has determined that the foregoing factors support a finding that the ends of justice served by granting a continuance outweigh the best interests of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial. Furthermore, the\nCourt finds that the failure to grant the requested continuance would deny counsel for the defendant the reasonable time necessary for effective preparation, taking into account the exercise of due diligence.\n\nThe Court finds the period of time from 1/21/2025 (the filing of the instant Motion) to the new trial date of 9/30/2025, constitutes a period of delay which shall be EXCLUDED in computing the time within which the trial\nin this case must commence pursuant to the Speedy Trial Act, 18 U.S.C. Sections 3161(h)(1)(D), (h)(7) (A), and (h)(7)(B)(i) & (iv).\n\nGovernment to prepare an appropriate stipulation and order regarding speedy trial within 7 days to Trader_Orders@hid.uscourts.gov.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nMotion Hearing re 108 MOTION to Continue Trial Date filed by Darren Patrick Riley held on 1/23/2025.\nGranting 108 Motion to Continue as to Darren Patrick Riley (1).\nJury Selection/Trial is CONTINUED to 09:00 AM on 9/30/2025 before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nTrial Conference is CONTINUED to 9/18/2025 10:00 AM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(FTR-CT CT 5 / 10:34 AM-10:41 AM)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER)\n(jni) (Entered: 01/23/2025)\n01/23/2025 113 THIRD AMENDED CRIMINAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 1/23/2025.\n(jni) (Entered: 01/23/2025)\n01/23/2025 115 AMENDED EP: MOTION HEARING regarding Defendant's [ECF 108 ] Defendant's Motion to Continue Trial Date (\"Motion\") as to DEFENDANT DARREN PATRICK RILEY had on 1/23/2025.\n\n... The Court finds the period of time from 1/23/2025 (motion hearing) to the new trial date of 9/30/2025, constitutes a period of delay which shall be EXCLUDED in computing the time within which the trial in this case\nmust commence pursuant to the Speedy Trial Act, 18 U.S.C. Sections 3161(h)(1)(D), (h)(7)(A), and (h)(7)(B)(i) & (iv).\n\n(FTR-CT CT 5 / 10:34 AM-10:41 AM)\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER)\n(jni) (Entered: 01/27/2025)\n01/24/2025 114 NOTICE OF ATTORNEY APPEARANCE Gwendelynn Bills appearing for USA. (Bills, Gwendelynn) (Entered: 01/24/2025)\n01/27/2025 116 ORDER CONTINUING TRIAL DATE AND EXCLUDING TIME UNDER THE SPEEDY TRIAL ACT as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 1/27/2025.\nDefendants Motion is GRANTED and IT IS HEREBY ORDERED:\n(1) Jury selection and trial are set for September 30, 2025 at 9:00 a.m.;\n(2) The District Judge's Trial Conference is set for September 18, 2025 at 10:00 a.m. before the Hon. J. Michael Seabright;\n(3) Dates previously scheduled are VACATED.\n\nIT IS FURTHER ORDERED that the period of time from January 23, 2025 to and including September 30, 2025, constitutes a period of delay which shall be excluded in computing the time within which the trial in this case must commence pursuant to the\nSpeedy Trial Act, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 3161(h)(7)(A) and (h)(7)(B)(iv).\n\n***Time Excluded as to Darren Patrick Riley: (1/23/2025-9/30/2025)\n(jni) (Entered: 01/27/2025)\n02/03/2025 117 EO: As to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley - In light of ORDER CONTINUING TRIAL DATE AND EXCLUDING TIME UNDER THE SPEEDY TRIAL ACT, ECF No. 119 , a Pretrial Conference is set for August 12,\n2025 at 10:00 AM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\nParties should consult the court's digital calendar on the hearing date for the courtroom assignment.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 02/03/2025)\n07/08/2025 118 EO: As to Darren Patrick Riley - Due to a conflict in the Court's calendar, the Pretrial Conference set for August 12, 2025 at 10:00 AM is moved to 03:00 PM on the same day in Aha Kanawai before JUDGE J. MICHAEL\nSEABRIGHT.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 07/08/2025)\n08/04/2025 119 EO: As to Darren Patrick Riley - at the Court's request, with the agreement of the parties, the Pretrial Conference set for August 12, 2025 at 03:00 PM is ADVANCED to Monday, August 11, 2025 at 11:00 AM in Aha\nKaulike Kanawai before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(rls) Modified on 8/4/2025 (rls). (Entered: 08/04/2025)\n08/07/2025 120 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Gary G. Singh. by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration of Counsel, # 2 Certificate of Service)(Singh, Gary) (Entered: 08/07/2025)\n08/07/2025 121 EO: The court will hear the Motion to Withdraw as Attorney, ECF No. 120 , on August 11, 2025, at 11:00 a.m. in Aha Kanawai. The government may file an optional response by 5:00 p.m. on August 8, 2025.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(rls) (Entered: 08/07/2025)\n08/08/2025 122 RESPONSE by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley re 120 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Gary G. Singh. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 08/08/2025)\n08/11/2025 123 EP: MOTION FOR WITHDRAWAL AS COUNSEL FOR DEFENDANT DARREN PATRICK RILEY held; TRIAL CONFERENCE not held.\n\nDefendant Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, present.\n\nDiscussion held.\n\n[11:02 - 11:12 am] SEALED HEARING. Courtroom cleared. Discussion held between the Court, Mr. Singh, and Defendant.\nHearing unsealed. AUSAs Perlmutter and Bills, and public return to the courtroom.\n\nFor reasons stated on the record, 120 MOTION FOR WITHDRAWAL AS COUNSEL FOR DEFENDANT DARREN PATRICK RILEY - GRANTED. Mr. Singh to prepare and submit an order. New counsel will be\nappointed.\n\nThe Court directed the parties to reach out to Magistrate Judge Porter's chambers to reschedule the September 30, 2025 trial date, once new counsel is appointed.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nMotion Hearing re 120 MOTION to Withdraw as Attorney by Gary G. Singh as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 8/11/2025.\nGranting 120 Motion to Withdraw as Attorney.\n\n(Reporter-Cynthia Fazio)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 08/11/2025)\n\n08/11/2025 124 ORDER GRANTING MOTION FOR WITHDRAWAL OF COUNSEL FOR DEFENDANT DARREN PATRICK RILEY re 120 - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT on 8/11/2025.\n(jni) (Entered: 08/11/2025)\n08/12/2025 125 CJA 20 as to Darren Patrick Riley: Appointment of Andrew M. Kennedy, Esq. - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER on 8/12/2025.\nSubs for Panel Attorney Gary Singh.\n(jni) (Entered: 08/12/2025)\n08/13/2025 126 EO: As noted in the Court's 8/11/2025 Minutes, ECF No. 123 , the Court intends to reschedule the 9/30/2025 trial date. Counsel are DIRECTED to meet and confer and submit a stipulation and order continuing the trial\ndate. The stipulation shall include two proposed agreed-upon trial dates and language excluding time under the Speedy Trial Act. The stipulation shall be submitted to porter_orders@hid.uscourts.gov no later than\n8/22/2025.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jo) (Entered: 08/13/2025)\n08/21/2025 127 STIPULATION CONTINUING TRIAL DATE AND EXCLUDING TIME UNDER THE SPEEDY TRIAL ACT; CERTIFICATE OF SERVICE as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES\nREBER PORTER on 8/21/2025.\n(1) Jury selection and trial are set for February 18, 2026, before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.;\n(2) Dates previously scheduled in ECF No. 113 are VACATED. The Court will issue a new scheduling order.\n\nIT IS FURTHER ORDERED that the period of time from September 30, 2025 to and including the newly set trial date of February 18, 2026, constitutes a period of delay which shall be excluded in computing the time within which the trial in this case must\ncommence pursuant to the Speedy Trial Act, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 3161(h)(7)(A) and (h)(7)(B).\n\nJury Selection/Trial is CONTINUED to 09:00 AM on 2/18/2026 before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n***Time Excluded as to Darren Patrick Riley: (9/30/2025-2/18/2026)\n(jni) (Entered: 08/21/2025)\n08/21/2025 128 EO: Pursuant to ECF No. 127 Stipulation Continuing Trial Date and Excluding Time Under the Speedy Trial Act, new dates and deadlines given. Court to issue a Fourth Amended Criminal Scheduling Order.\n\nTrial Dates and Deadlines:\nJury Selection/Jury Trial is set for 2/18/2026 9:00 AM before Judge JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT\nTrial Conference is set for 2/5/2026 10:00 AM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n(Please see attached Minutes for all trial dates and deadlines)\n\nTrial Conference CONTINUED to 2/5/2026 10:00 AM before Judge J. Michael Seabright.\n\n(MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER)\n(jni) (Entered: 08/21/2025)\n08/21/2025 129 FOURTH AMENDED CRIMINAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE WES REBER PORTER on 8/21/2025.\n(jni) (Entered: 08/21/2025)\n10/10/2025 130 Ex Parte APPLICATION by Darren Patrick Riley (Attachments: # 1 Declaration, # 2 Proposed Order)(Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 10/10/2025)\n10/10/2025 131 ORDER GRANTING: EX-PARTE MOTION FOR ORDER PERMITTING FDC HONOLULU TO RETRIEVE DISCOVERY DRIVE FROM DEFENDANT AND RETURN DRIVE TO DEFENSE COUNSEL as to\nDarren Patrick Riley re 130 - Signed by MAGISTRATE JUDGE ROM TRADER on 10/10/2025.\n(jni) (Entered: 10/10/2025)\n12/17/2025 132 EO: As to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley - At Defendant's request, and agreement by the Government, Trial Conference set for February 5, 2026 is CONTINUED to February 10, 2026 at 11:00 AM before JUDGE J.\nMICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\nParties should consult the court's digital calendar on the hearing date for the courtroom assignment.\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 12/17/2025)\n12/29/2025 133 EO: As to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley - A Status Conference is set for January 8, 2026 at 01:30 PM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 12/29/2025)\n01/07/2026 134 MOTION to Suppress Pretrial Motion No. 1: Motion to Suppress 2020 iphone (1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2) by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration Counsel, # 2 Declaration Darren Patrick Riley, # 3 Table\nof Contents, # 4 Table of Authorities, # 5 Memorandum in Support of Motion, # 6 Exhibit A1-A4 (Placeholder), # 7 Exhibit B, # 8 Exhibit C, # 9 Exhibit D, # 10 Exhibit E, # 11 Exhibit F, # 12 Certificate of Service)\n(Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 01/07/2026)\n01/07/2026 135 MOTION to Suppress Pretrial Motion No. 2: Motion to Suppress Seizure of Red Iphone (1B15) by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration, # 2 Table of Contents, # 3 Table of Authorities, # 4 Memorandum\nMemorandum in Support of Motion, # 5 Certificate of Service)(Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 01/07/2026)\n01/07/2026 136 MOTION for Hearing Pretrial Motion No. 3 Re: Motion For Franks Hearing As To SW 22-2101 by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Declaration Counsel, # 2 Table of Contents, # 3 Table of Authorities, # 4\nMemorandum in Support of Motion, # 5 Exhibit A, # 6 Exhibit B, # 7 Exhibit C (Placeholder), # 8 Exhibit D, # 9 Exhibit E, # 10 Certificate of Service)(Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 01/07/2026)\n01/08/2026 137 EP : Status Conference as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 1/8/2026. Defendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, present. Ms. Bills participated telephonically.\n\nA hearing on 135 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 2 Re: Motion to Suppress Seizure of Red iPhone (1B15); and 136 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 3 Re: Request for Franks Hearing Re: Motion to Suppress iPhone 13\nPro Max (1B10) is SET for January 21, 2026 at 1:30 p.m. before the Honorable J. Michael Seabright. Government's Responses are due by January 16, 2026. Witness and Exhibit Lists are due by January 19, 2026. If\nnecessary, the hearing will resume on January 22, 2026 at 10:00 a.m.\n\nA hearing on 134 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 1 Re: Defendant's Motion to Suppress 2020 iPhone (1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2); and is SET for February 18, 2026 at 9:30 a.m. before the Honorable J. Michael\nSeabright. Government's Responses are due by February 6, 2026. Witness and Exhibit Lists are due by February 16, 2026.\n\nMs. Bills may participate in the evidentiary hearings telephonically. However, she may not conduct oral argument.\n\nDiscussion held regarding the February 18, 2026 trial date. By agreement of the parties, Jury Selection/Jury Trial is CONTINUED to March 4, 2026.\n\nThe court finds that the ends of justice served by such an action outweigh the best interest of the public and the defendant in a speedy trial. Government to prepare a Stipulation and Order Continuing Trial Date and\nExcluding Time Under the Speedy Trial Act. All trial-related deadlines set in Criminal Scheduling Order, ECF No. 129 are VACATED. Court to issue a new Criminal Scheduling Order.\n\nGovernment states it will need 2 weeks for its case-in-chief at trial.\nDefendant will need 1 week for his case-in-chief at trial.\n\nThe parties agree to seat 15 jurors.\n\nTrial will be conducted from 8:30 a.m. to 2:00 p.m./2:30 p.m. with a modified lunch schedule.\n\nThe parties to meet and confer to discuss modifications, if any, to the Court's Proposed Juror Questionnaire and the publishing of trial exhibits during trial to the jury. Any comments on the court's proposed questionnaire is\ndue by January 15, 2026. A stipulation or statement (joint or individual) regarding the trial exhibits is due by January 22, 2026.\n\nThere being no objection to the Jury Questionnaire for Federal Jury Service, thequestionnaire will be mailed out on January 26, 2026.\n\nDefendant is remanded into the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nStatus Conference - DJ as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 1/8/2026;\n135 MOTION to Suppress Pretrial Motion No. 2: Motion to Suppress Seizure of Red Iphone (1B15) & 136 MOTION for Hearing Pretrial Motion No. 3 Re: Motion For Franks Hearing As To SW 22-2101 are set for 1/21/2026 01:30 PM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT;\n134 MOTION to Suppress Pretrial Motion No. 1: Motion to Suppress 2020 iphone (1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2) is set for 2/18/2026 09:30 AM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(Reporter-Beth Krupa (remote)) (JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(eta) (Entered: 01/09/2026)\n01/09/2026 138 SECOND STIPULATION CONTINUING TRIAL DATE AND EXCLUDING TIME UNDER THE SPEEDY TRIAL ACT; CERTIFICATE OF SERVICE as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL\nSEABRIGHT on 1/9/2026.\n\n(1) Jury selection and trial are set for the March 4, 2026, at 9:00 a.m.;\n\n(2) Dates previously scheduled are VACATED. The Court will issue a new scheduling order.\n\nIT IS FURTHER ORDERED that the period of time from February 18, 2026 to and including March 4, 2026, constitutes a period of delay which shall be excluded in computing the time within which the trial in this case must commence pursuant to the\nSpeedy Trial Act, 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 3161(h)(7)(A) and (h)(7)(B)(iv).\n\nJury Selection/Trial is CONTINUED to 09:00 AM on 3/4/2026 before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n***Time Excluded as to Darren Patrick Riley: (2/18/2026-3/4/2026)\n(jni) (Entered: 01/09/2026)\n01/09/2026 139 FIFTH AMENDED CRIMINAL SCHEDULING ORDER as to Darren Patri