Motions in Limine are now due on February 3, 2026, Replies are due on February 12, 2026.\n\nDefendant's Witness:\n1. Darren Patrick Riley (CST for Direct, Cross, Re-Direct examination)\n\nDefendant rests.\n\nGovernment's Witness:\n1. Gabriel Keown (CST for Direct and Cross Examination)\n\nGovernment Admitted Exhibits: A through L\n\nGovernment rests.\n\nDiscussion held.\n\nContinued hearing on 135 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 2 Re: Motion to Suppress Seizure of Red iPhone (1B15) is SET for January 22, 2026 at 10:00 AM in Aha Kanawai before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nMs. Bills may participate by telephone.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\n\n(Reporter-Gloria Bediamol)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(shm) (Entered: 01/21/2026)\n01/22/2026 159 EP: Continued hearing on DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 2 RE: MOTION TO SUPPRESS SEIZURE OF RED IPHONE (1B15) held.\n\nDefendant Riley, in custody, present.\n\nMs. Bills participated by telephone.\n\nFBI SA Sherwin Chang was also present.\n\nGovernment's Exhibit Received: O.\n\nLegal discussion held. Oral arguments heard.\n\nFor reason stated on the record, 135 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 2 Re: Motion to Suppress Seizure of Red iPhone (1B15)-DENIED.\n\nDefendant remanded to the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nContinued Motion Hearing re 135 Motion to Suppress Seizure of Red Iphone (1B15) filed by Darren Patrick Riley held on 1/22/2026.\nDenying 135 Motion to Suppress as to Darren Patrick Riley.\n\n(Reporter-Gloria Bediamol)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 01/22/2026)\n01/22/2026 160 ORDER DENYING DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 2 RE: MOTION TO SUPPRESS SEIZURE OF RED IPHONE (1B15), ECF NO. 135 as to Darren Patrick Riley re 135 - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL\nSEABRIGHT on 1/22/2026.\n(jni) (Entered: 01/22/2026)\n01/22/2026 161 ORDER DENYING DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 3 RE: MOTION TO SUPPRESS IPHONE 13 PRO MAX (1B10), ECF NO. 136 as to Darren Patrick Riley re 136 - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL\nSEABRIGHT on 1/22/2026.\n(jni) (Entered: 01/22/2026)\n01/27/2026 162 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Pretrial Motion No. 4 by Darren Patrick Riley. (Attachments: # 1 Proposed Motion and Exhibits, # 2 Certificate of Service)(Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 01/27/2026)\n01/28/2026 163 EO: Defendant Darren Patrick Riley's Motion to Extend Pretrial Motions Deadline Re: Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 4, ECF No. 162 , is GRANTED in part. \"Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 4 Re Second Motion to\nSuppress 2020 iPhone (1B1),\" ECF No. [162-1], is deemed FILED. The government is directed to respond by February 6, 2026--the same date by which a response to Defendant's first Motion to Suppress 2020 iPhone\n(1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2), ECF No. 134 , is due. The court recognizes that this provides little time for the government to respond. Accordingly, if the government believes more time is needed, it may file a motion to\nextend the deadline to respond by January 30, 2026.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 01/28/2026)\n02/02/2026 164 STIPULATION Parties' Stipulation Regarding Evidentiary Matters; COS (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/02/2026)\n02/03/2026 165 NOTICE Governments Notice Of Intent To Use Evidence Pursuant To Rule 414; COS by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/03/2026)\n02/03/2026 166 MOTION in Limine No. 1 Re: Narration of Videos by Darren Patrick Riley. (Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 02/03/2026)\n02/05/2026 167 EO: In case as to Defendant Darren Patrick Riley - Hearing on 162 Motion for Extension of Time to File Pretrial Motion No. 4 is set for February 6, 2026 at 01:30 PM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL\nSEABRIGHT. Mr. Kennedy and Ms. Bills may appear by telephone.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 02/05/2026)\n02/05/2026 168 STIPULATION AND ORDER EXTENDING DEADLINE FOR DEFENDANT RILEY TO FILE DEFENDANT'S MOTION IN LIMINE 2 RE: RESPONSE TO GOVERNMENT 404(b) NOTICE [Filed January 20,\n2026] as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT on 2/5/2026.\n(jni) (Entered: 02/05/2026)\n02/06/2026 169 MOTION in Limine No. 2 Re: Opposition to Government 404(b) Notice by Darren Patrick Riley. (Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 02/06/2026)\n02/06/2026 170 EP: Hearing on 162 Motion for Extension of Time to File Pretrial Motion No. 4 as to Defendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley was not held; Status Conference held.\n\nDefendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, present.\n\nMs. Bills and Mr. Kennedy participated telephonically.\n\nDiscussion held regarding upcoming deadlines, witnesses to be called at the 2/18/2026 evidentiary hearing, and juror questionnaire.\n\nAn Evidentiary Hearing on 134 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 1 Re: Defendant's Motion to Suppress 2020 iPhone (1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2); and 162 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 4 Re: Defendant's Second Motion\nto Suppress 2020 iPhone (1B1) is SET for February 18, 2026 at 9:30 a.m. before the Honorable J. Michael Seabright. Government's Responses are due on February 6, 2026.\n\nHearing on 166 Defendant's Motion in Limine No. 1 Re: Narration of Videos; and 169 Defendant's Motion in Limine 2 Re: Opposition to Government 404(b) Notice [Filed January 20, 2026] is SET for February 25, 2026\nat 1:30 p.m. before the Honorable J. Michael Seabright. Government's Responses are due on February 18, 2026.\n\nFinal Pretrial Conference set for February 19, 2026 is CONTINUED to February 25, 2026 at 1:30 p.m. before the Honorable J. Michael Seabright.\n\nThe parties should consult the court's digital calendar on the hearing date(s) for the courtroom assignment.\n\nDefendant is remanded into the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nStatus Conference - DJ as to Darren Patrick Riley held on 2/6/2026 in case as to Darren Patrick Riley.\nMotion Hearing re 134 , 162 is set for 2/18/2026 09:30 AM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nMotion Hearing re 166 , 169] is set for 2/25/2026 01:30 PM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nEvidentiary Hearing is set for 2/18/2026 09:30 AM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nPretrial Conference is CONTINUED to 2/25/2026 01:30 PM before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(Reporter-Beth Krupa)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 02/06/2026)\n02/06/2026 171 RESPONSE in Opposition by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley re 162 MOTION for Extension of Time to File Pretrial Motion No. 4 (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit A (report), # 2 Exhibit B (email))(Perlmutter, Rebecca)\n(Entered: 02/06/2026)\n02/06/2026 172 RESPONSE in Opposition by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley re 134 MOTION to Suppress Pretrial Motion No. 1: Motion to Suppress 2020 iphone (1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2) (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit 1 (inventory\nphotos), # 2 Exhibit 2 (suitcase photos), # 3 Exhibit 3 (video placeholder), # 4 Exhibit 4 (video placeholder))(Perlmutter, Rebecca)\nExhibits 3 and 4 (CDs) to be retained by the Clerk's Office. Modified on 2/11/2026 (jni) (Entered: 02/06/2026)\n\n02/11/2026 173 Joint Proposed Jury Instructionsby USA as toDarren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) Modified on 2/12/2026 (jni) (Entered: 02/11/2026)\n02/11/2026 174 Joint Proposed Verdict Formby USA as toDarren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) Modified on 2/12/2026 (jni) (Entered: 02/11/2026)\n02/13/2026 175 EO: During the upcoming February 18, 2026 hearing, the parties should be prepared to discuss what procedures may be necessary and appropriate to promote candor while protecting prospective jurors' privacy during\nvoir dire, given the sensitive nature of the subjects covered in the special juror questionnaire. See Press-Enter. Co. v. Superior Ct. of Cal., Riverside Cnty., 464 U.S. 501, 51011 (1984) (stating that the presumption of\nopenness of criminal trials \"may be overcome only by an overriding interest,\" such as when voir dire \"touches on deeply personal matters\" that a prospective juror may have \"legitimate reasons for keeping out of the\npublic domain\"). Specifically, the parties should be prepared to discuss whether limited sealing may be appropriate, and if so, what procedures should be followed. See id. at 51012 (stating that sealing of voir dire should\nbe (1) based on a prospective juror's affirmative request, (2) supported by findings establishing necessity, and (3) narrowly tailored).\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 02/13/2026)\n02/16/2026 176 EXHIBIT LIST ECF 134 and 162, Defendant's Pretrial Motions No. 1, 4 Re: LAX Interview by Darren Patrick Riley. (Kennedy, Andrew) Modified on 2/17/2026 (jni) (Entered: 02/16/2026)\n02/16/2026 177 WITNESS LIST ECF 134 and 162, Defendant's Pretrial Motions No. 1, 4 Re: LAX Interview by Darren Patrick Riley. (Kennedy, Andrew) Modified on 2/17/2026 (jni) (Entered: 02/16/2026)\n02/16/2026 178 EXHIBIT LIST RE: DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 1, MOTION TO SUPPRESS 1B1 AND 1B2, ECF NO. 134 by USA as toDarren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) Modified on 2/17/2026 (jni) (Entered: 02/16/2026)\n02/16/2026 179 WITNESS LIST RE: DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 1, MOTION TO SUPPRESS 1B1 AND 1B2, ECF NO. 134 by USA as toDarren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) Modified on 2/17/2026 (jni) (Entered:\n02/16/2026)\n02/17/2026 180 EO: To clarify for the parties, because the facts of the two pending motions to suppress, ECF Nos. 134 and 162 , are factually intertwined, the evidentiary hearing set for February 18, 2026 will cover both motions.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 02/17/2026)\n02/17/2026 181 EO: The court will soon be sending the parties a copy of the September 12, 2020 Warrant Application, ECF No.134-7 at PageID.631677. The court has highlighted the portions of the probable cause affidavit that the court\nhas determined are based on statements made by Mr. Riley after he invoked his right to counsel. The parties should review the affidavit before the upcoming hearing and be prepared to discuss whether the court has\ncorrectly identified the highlighted portions as being based on post-invocation statements.\n\nThe court has reviewed the entire recording of the interview with Mr. Riley; the parties should limit playback of the recording during the hearing accordingly, focusing only on pertinent excerpts.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 02/17/2026)\n02/18/2026 182 ORDER DENYING DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 1 RE: MOTION TO SUPPRESS 2020 IPHONE (1B1) AND 2020 IPAD (1B2), ECF NO. 134 as to Darren Patrick Riley re 134 - Signed by JUDGE J.\nMICHAEL SEABRIGHT on 2/18/2026.\n(jni) (Entered: 02/18/2026)\n02/18/2026 183 ORDER DENYING DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 4 RE: SECOND MOTION TO SUPPRESS 2020 IPHONE (1B1), ECF NO. 162-1 as to Darren Patrick Riley re 162 - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL\nSEABRIGHT on 2/18/2026.\n(jni) (Entered: 02/18/2026)\n02/18/2026 184 EVIDENTIARY HEARING\n\nEP: Hearing on 134 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 1 Re: Defendant's Motion to Suppress 2020 iPhone (1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2); and 162 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 4 Re: Defendant's Second Motion to Suppress\n2020 iPhone (1B1) as to Defendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley held.\n\nDefendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley, in custody, present.\n\nFBI SA Sherwin Chang was also present.\n\nDiscussion held.\n\nHearing on Motions in Limine 166 and 169 and the Final Pretrial Conference set for February 25, 2026 at 1:30 p.m. is CONTINUED to 2:30 p.m. on the SAME DAY in Aha Kaulike before the Honorable J. Michael\nSeabright. Government's Response to 169 Defendant's Motion in Limine 2 is due by Saturday, February 21, 2026.\n\nGovernment's Witnesses:\n1. Marlon Coronado (CST for Direct and Cross Examination)\n2. Shawna Candelaria (CST for Direct and Cross Examination)\n\nGovernment Admitted Exhibits: 1 through 10\n\nGovernment rests.\n\nDefendant's Witness:\n1. Darren Patrick Riley (CST for Direct and Cross examination)\nDefendant rests.\n\nOral arguments heard.\n\n134 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 1 Re: Defendant's Motion to Suppress 2020 iPhone (1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2) - DENIED.\n\n162 Defendant's Pretrial Motion No. 4 Re: Defendant's Second Motion to Suppress 2020 iPhone (1B1) - DENIED.\n\nDiscussion was held regarding the juror questionnaire and the procedures to be implemented during jury selection. The parties are directed to meet and confer and to submit a joint statement setting forth the proposed\nprocess to be conducted during jury selection, to Judge Seabright's orders box no later than Monday, February 23, 2026.\n\nDefendant is remanded into the custody of the U.S. Marshals Service.\nMotion Hearing re: 134 MOTION to Suppress Pretrial Motion No. 1: Motion to Suppress 2020 iphone (1B1) and 2020 iPad (1B2) held on 2/18/2026.\nDenying 134 Pretrial Motion No. 1 as to Darren Patrick Riley.\nMotion Hearing re 162 MOTION No. 4 Re: Defendant's Second Motion to Suppress 2020 iPhone (1B1) held on 2/18/2026.\nDenying 162 MOTION No. 4 as to Darren Patrick Riley.\nMotion Hearing re 166 , 169 is CONTINUED to 2/25/2026 02:30 PM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\nFinal Pretrial Conference DJ is CONTINUED to 2/25/2026 02:30 PM in Aha Kaulike before JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT.\n\n(Reporter-Cynthia Fazio)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)\n(jni) (Entered: 02/18/2026)\n02/18/2026 185 GOVERNMENT'S AMENDED EXHIBIT LIST RE: DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 1, MOTION TO SUPPRESS 1B1 AND 1B2, ECF NO. 134, AND DEFENDANT'S PRETRIAL MOTION NO. 4, MOTION TO\nSUPPRESS IPHONE (1B1), ECF NO. 162 by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley. (Bills, Gwendelynn) Modified on 2/19/2026 (jni) (Entered: 02/18/2026)\n02/18/2026 186 RESPONSE to Motion by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley re 166 MOTION in Limine No. 1 Re: Narration of Videos (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/18/2026)\n02/20/2026 187 Proposed Voir Direby USA as toDarren Patrick Riley. (Bills, Gwendelynn) (Entered: 02/20/2026)\n02/20/2026 188 TRIAL BRIEFby USA as toDarren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/20/2026)\n02/21/2026 189 RESPONSE by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley re 169 MOTION in Limine No. 2 Re: Opposition to Government 404(b) Notice (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/21/2026)\n02/23/2026 190 REQUEST for Realtime Court Reporting Services for Jury Selection/Trial set for March 4, 2026. (rlfh) (Entered: 02/23/2026)\n02/23/2026 191 EO: Regarding Request for Realtime Court Reporting Services for Jury Selection/Trial set for March 4, 2026.\n\nWitness and exhibit lists shall be filed by February 24, 2026.\n\nTrial exhibits shall be marked with an exhibit number. The parties should meet and confer to discuss the exhibit numbering to avoid duplication of exhibit numbers.\n\nCourtesy copies for the court: Three (3) copies of exhibits placed in 3-ring binder(s) with tabs delivered to the Clerk's office by February 24, 2026. The spine of the 3-ring binder(s) shall not exceed 2-3/4 inches, and shall\nbe clearly marked and labeled with the case name, binder volume, and range of exhibits contained in the binder.\n\nA digital copy of exhibits shall be submitted on a USB Drive, DVD-R or CD to the Clerk's office by February 24, 2026. Parties shall review the attached overview of the Jury Evidence Recording Systems (JERS), which\nprovides more information as to the acceptable file types, file size, etc.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(rlfh) (Entered: 02/23/2026)\n02/24/2026 192 EXHIBIT LISTby USA as toDarren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/24/2026)\n02/24/2026 193 WITNESS LISTby USA as toDarren Patrick Riley. (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/24/2026)\n02/24/2026 194 WITNESS LIST by Darren Patrick Riley. (Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 02/24/2026)\n02/24/2026 195 EXHIBIT LIST by Darren Patrick Riley. (Kennedy, Andrew) (Entered: 02/24/2026)\n02/25/2026 196 NOTICE of FRE 902(11) and Public Records Certifications by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley (Attachments: # 1 Exhibit A (Certifications))(Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/25/2026)\n02/25/2026 197 EP: Hearing on Motions in Limine 166 and 169 ; Final Pretrial Conference as to Defendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley was not held; Status conference held.\n\nDefendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley refused to be transported to Court for this hearing.\n\nUSMS Stewart Yano and Ms. Becky Collingwood from FDC Honolulu informed the Court regarding Defendant's status.\n\nDiscussion held.\n\nHearing on Motions in Limine 166 and 169 and Final Pretrial Conference is SET for 2/26/2026 at 9:00 AM in Aha Kaulike before the Honorable J. Michael Seabright\n(Reporter-Ann Matsumoto)\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(shm) (Entered: 02/25/2026)\n02/25/2026 198 NOTICE Joint Trial Presentation Statement by USA as to Darren Patrick Riley (Perlmutter, Rebecca) (Entered: 02/25/2026)\n02/26/2026 199 ORDER TO PRODUCE as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT on 2/26/2026.\n(jni) (Entered: 02/26/2026)\n02/26/2026 200 AMENDED ORDER TO PRODUCE as to Darren Patrick Riley - Signed by JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT on 2/26/2026.\n(jni) (Entered: 02/26/2026)\n02/26/2026 201 EO: in case as to Darren Patrick Riley, since the courthouse closed due to a safety hazard, hearing on Motions in Limine 166 and 169 and Final Pretrial Conference is CONTINUED to 2/27/2026 at 2:30 PM in Aha\nKaulike before the Honorable J. Michael Seabright.\n\n(JUDGE J. MICHAEL SEABRIGHT)(shm) (Entered: 02/26/2026)\n02/26/2026 202 STIPULATION Parties' Joint Concise Statement (Bills, Gwendelynn) (Entered: 02/26/2026)\n02/26/2026 206 EP: Hearing on Motions in Limine 166 and 169 ; Final Pretrial Conference as to Defendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley was not held; Status Conference held.\n\nDefendant (01) Darren Patrick Riley refused to be transported to Court for this hearing.\n\nUSMS Stewart Yano and Ms. Becky Collingwood from FDC Honolulu inf"
